# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=conquest spec=paladin:protection
# style=idle view=390x844,touch save=fresh.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl first: conquest has one prior true idle-style match
# (2026-10-01-20.play, priest:shadow) confirming direction.md's #7 -- a body
# that presses and moves nothing takes zero damage all match while the team
# loses around it. That reading is a squishy ranged dps. No tank spec has
# ever been put through idle on any battleground, and no paladin:protection
# pull of any kind has ever happened on conquest specifically (its one prior
# battleground reading was style=melee on escort). A tank carries far more
# max hp and passive mitigation than a shadow priest, which is the one thing
# that could make "idle survives untouched" break down differently here: a
# body too big and too slow to be worth the AI's notice stays alive on both
# readings so far, but a tank is also the class the role-count roll most
# wants anchoring a point -- worth seeing whether an idle tank still gets
# treated as irrelevant or gets converged on simply for standing nearer the
# fight. Three chunks with `bill` after each, same shape as the priest run,
# so the two are a same-map, same-style, cross-role comparison rather than a
# one-off.
open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
targets
shot bg-menu

tap map:conquest
targets
shot conquest-picked

tap class:paladin:protection
shot class-picked

tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play idle 90
shot mid1
state
bill
says

wait 5
play idle 90
shot mid2
state
bill

wait 5
play idle 90
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
